# Auto Email Campaign schedule, run by supercronic in the `campaign` compose service.
# Times are in the container's TZ (Asia/Kolkata). Each job takes its own Postgres
# advisory lock and exits if another run holds it, so overlapping runs are harmless.
# Add --dry-run to a line to watch it without writing anything.

# daily: every 15 minutes (it was 06:30 IST once a day until 2026-10-19), so new CRM data is picked up within 15 minutes.
# The whole pipeline for every allowed source (not the held-out GoodFirms/Clutch batches) and crm.CrmLeads:
# intake, free checks, domain, scan, score gate, report, contact ranking, NeverBounce, drafting, and the AE_
# write. It repeats until nothing moves (or AE_DAILY_MAX_HOURS), and skips whatever is already done.
# A run that is still going when the next tick comes makes that tick exit at once (the job's advisory lock), so runs never
# overlap. NeverBounce is live in this service (docker-compose.yml), with its daily credit cap (AE_NEVERBOUNCE_DAILY_CREDIT_CAP).
*/15 * * * * cd /app && python -m campaign.jobs daily

# housekeeping: 02:00 IST. Reconciliation (takes in anything intake missed) and the read-only mirror audit.
0 2 * * * cd /app && python -m campaign.jobs housekeeping
